                            <h3>Introduction</h3>
                            <p><p align="justify">The MPA (Theatre Arts)  at School of Performing and Visual Arts,  Indira Gandhi National Open University(IGNOU)consists both theoreticalandpracticalcoursesthatprovideawider perceptiontothe learners enrolling in the programme. It consists of 16 courses spread over two yearsin addition to dissertation in the second year. The MPA in Theatre Arts  will be offered in a modular format with exit and later entry options. Learners have the option to exit after completing the first year.Those who wish to avail this option receive the Post Graduate Theatre Arts. Those who complete the second year receive an MPA Theatre Arts Degree.<br/>

The programme, in general, is divided into four semesters.  In each semester two practical courses clubbed with theory courses and a dissertation in fourth semester a dissertation. <br/>

The programme designed in a such a way that the  learners will gain both theoretical and practical knowledge of Theatre Arts and as well as provide a foundation to Film Acting which is in more demand in today’s scenario. Further the learners will be able to create theatrical performances and also will be able to earn their employment either in private or in public sector.  Thisprogramme will also provide an introduction to Research methodology for those who are interested to do researchPerforming Arts (Theatre and its allied arts)</p>
</p>
                            <h3>Objective</h3>
                            <p><p align="justify">The programme aims to provide advanced theoretical and practical training and also professional development. In keeping with the goals set by New Education Policy (NEP), the programme's objectives are:
<ul>
<li>To provide theoretical and practical aspects of Theatre Arts.</li>
<li>To familiarize learners with the  techniques of Art of Theatre such as Acting, Direction, Technical Aspects and also the world of Arts and Aesthetics.</li>
<li>To introduce learners to the histories of both Indian and Western and also to the contemporary developments of Theatre in India.</li>
<li>To encourage learners towards creative theatrical performances through productions and short films.</li></ul></p>
</p>
